# Brewfile — Homebrew prerequisites for the Mac mini homelab hub.
#
# Captures the OS-level packages the homelab infra depends on, so a
# from-bare-macOS rebuild is `brew bundle` instead of "remember what to install".
# Run: `brew bundle --file infra/Brewfile` (mini-setup.sh does this for you).
#
# This is the ONE gap mini-setup.sh / bootstrap.sh don't cover on their own:
# they assume brew + these packages already exist. This file closes it.
#
# NOT captured here (can't be — see infra/README.md "Prerequisites"):
#   - Homebrew itself       (bootstrap: the install-from-curl one-liner)
#   - Tailscale.app         (Mac App Store GUI build, root-owned — not a brew cask)
#   - Xcode Command Line Tools (`xcode-select --install` — gives git + make for
#                               the osx-cpu-temp build)
# Only homelab-infra deps live here; the operator's own tooling (opencode, node,
# p7zip) is intentionally left out so this file stays a truthful infra manifest.

# --- container runtime -------------------------------------------------------
cask "orbstack"        # Docker/Compose engine — every infra/ stack runs on this

# --- host metrics ------------------------------------------------------------
brew "node_exporter"   # darwin host metrics → VictoriaMetrics (mini-metrics scrapes it)

# --- secrets (observability backend) ----------------------------------------
brew "sops"            # decrypts the sops-encrypted backend secrets
brew "age"             # sops backend key for that decryption
